# Styling Conventions for Treinoway Web

## Use Existing CSS Variables

Always use the CSS design tokens defined in `src/index.css`. Do not hardcode colors, spacing, or other values:

```css
/* ✅ CORRECT */
.my-component {
  color: var(--color-primary);
  padding: var(--spacing-md);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  font-size: var(--font-body-size);
  background-color: var(--color-surface);
}

/* ❌ WRONG */
.my-component {
  color: #0055FF;
  padding: 16px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 16px;
  background-color: #F9FAFB;
}
```

## Available Design Tokens

### Colors
```css
/* Primary colors */
--color-primary
--color-on-primary
--color-primary-container
--color-on-primary-container

/* Secondary colors */
--color-secondary
--color-on-secondary
--color-secondary-container
--color-on-secondary-container

/* Tertiary colors */
--color-tertiary
--color-on-tertiary
--color-tertiary-container
--color-on-tertiary-container

/* Surface colors */
--color-surface
--color-on-surface
--color-surface-container
--color-surface-container-high

/* Error colors */
--color-error
--color-on-error
--color-error-container
--color-on-error-container

/* Success colors (custom) */
--color-success
--color-on-success
--color-success-container
--color-on-success-container

/* Outline */
--color-outline
--color-outline-variant
```

### Spacing
```css
--spacing-xs: 4px
--spacing-sm: 8px
--spacing-md: 16px
--spacing-lg: 24px
--spacing-xl: 32px
--spacing-xxl: 48px
```

### Border Radius
```css
--radius-xs: 4px
--radius-sm: 8px
--radius-md: 12px
--radius-lg: 16px
--radius-xl: 24px
--radius-full: 9999px
```

### Typography
```css
/* Font family */
--font-family-base: "Poppins", sans-serif

/* Headings */
--font-h1-size: 24px
--font-h1-weight: 700
--font-h2-size: 20px
--font-h2-weight: 600
--font-h3-size: 18px
--font-h3-weight: 500

/* Body text */
--font-body-size: 16px
--font-body-weight: 400
--font-body-large-size: 18px
--font-body-small-size: 14px

/* Button labels */
--font-button-label-size: 14px
--font-button-label-weight: 600
--font-button-label-letter-spacing: 1.25px

/* Caption */
--font-caption-size: 12px
--font-caption-weight: 400
```

### Shadows
```css
--shadow-sm: 0px 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)
--shadow-md: 0px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)
--shadow-lg: 0px 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15)
```

## Use Existing Utility Classes

The project has predefined utility classes in `src/index.css`. Use them instead of creating new styles:

### Cards
```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<div className="card">
  <h2 className="card-title">Title</h2>
  <p className="card-description">Description</p>
</div>

<div className="card card--mb">Content with margin bottom</div>
```

### Buttons
```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<button className="btn-primary">Primary Action</button>
<button className="btn-secondary">Secondary Action</button>
<button className="btn-logout">Logout</button>

// Disabled state
<button className="btn-primary" disabled={loading}>
  {loading ? 'Loading...' : 'Submit'}
</button>
```

### Form Inputs
```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<input type="text" className="form-input" placeholder="Nome" />
<textarea className="form-input" rows={4} />
<select className="form-input">
  <option>Select...</option>
</select>
```

### Alerts
```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<div className="alert alert-success">Success message!</div>
<div className="alert alert-error">Error message!</div>
```

### Badges
```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<span className="badge">New</span>
<span className="badge badge-success">Active</span>
<span className="badge badge-error">Inactive</span>
```

## No External CSS Frameworks

Do not use Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, Material-UI, or any other CSS framework:

```jsx
// ❌ WRONG
<div className="bg-blue-500 p-4 rounded-lg">Content</div>
<Button variant="contained" color="primary">Click</Button>

// ✅ CORRECT
<div className="card">Content</div>
<button className="btn-primary">Click</button>
```

## No CSS-in-JS

Do not use styled-components, emotion, or inline styles (except for exceptional cases):

```jsx
// ❌ WRONG
import styled from 'styled-components';
const Button = styled.button`
  background: blue;
  padding: 16px;
`;

// ❌ WRONG (except for dynamic values)
<div style={{ color: 'blue', padding: '16px' }}>Content</div>

// ✅ CORRECT
<div className="card">Content</div>

// ✅ CORRECT (dynamic values are acceptable)
<div style={{ width: `${progress}%` }}>Progress bar</div>
```

## Font Usage

The project uses **Poppins** from Google Fonts. Do not change the font family:

```css
/* ✅ CORRECT */
body {
  font-family: var(--font-family-base);
}

/* ❌ WRONG */
body {
  font-family: 'Roboto', sans-serif;
}
```

## Responsive Design

Use media queries for responsive design. Common breakpoints:

```css
/* Mobile first approach */
.component {
  /* Mobile styles */
  padding: var(--spacing-sm);
}

/* Tablet */
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .component {
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
  }
}

/* Desktop */
@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  .component {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
}
```

## BEM-like Naming Convention

Use BEM-like naming for custom CSS classes:

```css
/* ✅ CORRECT */
.card { }
.card--highlighted { }
.card__title { }
.card__title--large { }

.sidebar { }
.sidebar--open { }
.sidebar--closed { }
.sidebar-link { }
.sidebar-link--active { }

/* ❌ WRONG */
.cardHighlighted { }
.Card-Title { }
.card_title_large { }
```

## Material 3 Design System

Follow Material 3 design principles:

- Use elevation (shadows) sparingly
- Prefer rounded corners with design tokens
- Use semantic colors (primary, secondary, error, success)
- Maintain consistent spacing scale
- Follow typography hierarchy

```css
/* ✅ CORRECT - Material 3 style */
.card {
  background-color: var(--color-surface);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: var(--spacing-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
}

.btn-primary {
  background-color: var(--color-primary);
  color: var(--color-on-primary);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  padding: var(--spacing-sm) var(--spacing-md);
  font-weight: var(--font-button-label-weight);
}
```
